---
pagination:
  data: cards
  size: 1
  alias: card
permalink: "/cards/{{ card.id }}/index.html"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ card.name }}"
  description: "What the Elixir record holds about {{ card.name }} in Clash Royale: how often it is played, how often it wins, by mode and by season."
  canonical: "/cards/{{ card.id }}"
layout: base.njk
---
{#- A card's record, PUBLIC and sign-in free: this is where a forwarded
    Card of the Week lands. The catalog facts are baked at build time and
    read true with JavaScript off; cards-live.js fills the season numbers
    from /api/public/cards/<id>, which the nightly rollup refreshes. -#}
<div class="page-head">
  <div style="display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap">
    <img
      src="/assets/cards/{{ card.id }}-160.png"
      alt="{{ card.name }}"
      width="160"
      height="236"
      style="border-radius: 10px"
      onerror="this.style.display='none'"
    />
    <div>
      <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 6px">{{ card.name }}</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin: 0; max-width: 60ch">
        {{ card.rarity | capitalize }} {{ card.type }}{% if card.elixir %}, {{ card.elixir }} elixir{% endif %}{% if card.forms.length %} &middot; {{ card.forms | join(" and ") }} form{% if card.forms.length > 1 %}s{% endif %}{% endif %}.
      </p>
      <p class="footnote" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
        Card <span class="mono">{{ card.id }}</span> &middot;
        <a href="/docs/cards">how a card is counted</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="panel" data-card="{{ card.id }}">
  <div class="panel__body">
    <h2 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 17px">This season</h2>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 4px; color: var(--ink-body)">
      Played in <strong data-card-live="usage">&mdash;</strong> of decided
      battles by <strong data-card-live="players">&mdash;</strong> recorded
      players, winning <strong data-card-live="win">&mdash;</strong>.
    </p>
    <p class="footnote" style="margin: 8px 0 0">
      A card&rsquo;s win rate describes who played it as much as the card.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" style="margin-top: 16px">
  <div class="panel__body">
    <h2 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 17px">By season</h2>
    <div data-card-live="history"><p class="footnote" style="margin: 0">Loading the record&hellip;</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" style="margin-top: 16px">
  <div class="panel__body">
    <h2 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 17px">By mode</h2>
    <div data-card-live="modes"><p class="footnote" style="margin: 0">Loading the record&hellip;</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" style="margin-top: 16px" data-card-live="issue" hidden>
  <div class="panel__body">
    <h2 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 17px">Card of the Week</h2>
    <p style="margin: 0" data-card-live="issue-line"></p>
  </div>
</section>

<p class="footnote" style="margin-top: 22px">
  Ask your own agent &ldquo;how am I doing with {{ card.name }}?&rdquo; once
  your tag is tracked. <a href="/">Request an account</a> &middot;
  <a href="/docs/email">the weekly email</a>
</p>

<script defer src="{{ "/assets/cards-live.js" | asset }}"></script>
